{"status":"completed","summary":"Restored /srv/legacy2/mail-filter-routing/bin/deliver. It securely routes RFC822 input by case-insensitive X-Department header name, preserves message bytes, and creates unique Maildir deliveries. Functionality and persistence were verified across a node1 reboot.","actions_performed":["Replaced the general-only, fixed-filename script with a POSIX shell implementation compatible with RHEL 10.","Created accounts, support, and general Maildir cur/new/tmp structures with restrictive permissions.","Verified routing using the staged samples, including lowercase and uppercase header names.","Verified byte-for-byte integrity with cmp and SHA-256 hashes.","Verified repeated-subject messages remain separate deliveries.","Rebooted node1 safely and verified recovery with a changed boot identity and a successful post-reboot delivery.","Retained all three staged sample files; no temporary staging files remain.","Kept RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 unchanged."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Restore a compatible executable mail-processing entry point","command_ids":["cmd-dd982fd6d7244606","cmd-e0b75347187c4e51"],"summary":"Diagnosed the defective fixed-name script, installed the replacement atomically, and validated its syntax, ownership, permissions, and SELinux context."},{"requirement":"Route accounts, support, and untagged messages correctly with case-insensitive header names","command_ids":["cmd-e61ddee3117f45aa","cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b"],"summary":"The uppercase accounts header routed to accounts, lowercase support header routed to support, and the untagged sample routed to general."},{"requirement":"Preserve message bytes and keep repeated subjects as separate deliveries","command_ids":["cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b"],"summary":"cmp and SHA-256 proved every delivery byte-identical to its source; two general messages with the same subject existed under distinct filenames."},{"requirement":"Retain staged samples and leave secure, clean state","command_ids":["cmd-5153fd7c65c54c7b","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"],"summary":"All three samples remain unchanged, staging directories are empty, mailbox directories are mode 0700, and delivered messages are mode 0600."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-dd982fd6d7244606","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"],"summary":"Before and after work, node1 remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c66a3eabfa83404d","cmd-c08f1b4381d1472c","cmd-e0ca20957fe84582","cmd-f584e6a502ae4433"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID 655710bc-9cfe-438a-903c-6fe21aee76a4 was captured with healthy data; reboot was acknowledged; boot ID changed to f98ddbec-ee9d-46bb-9b0f-b752923cd735; system health, stored deliveries, samples, and a fresh post-reboot support delivery were verified."}]}
